 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Common refinement",
 "statement": "Two stratifications $(\\iota_k\\colon Z_k\\to X)_{k<n}$ and\n$(\\kappa_l\\colon W_l\\to X)_{l<m}$ of a scheme $X$ have a common refinement.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-proper-base-change/sk-thm-properbasechange/lemma-constructible-common-refinement.md",
  "place": "node lemma-constructible-common-refinement, order 1293"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-constructible-refines",
  "def-constructible-stratification"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "Index the pairs $(k,l)$ by $k+nl<nm$. The intersections $X_k\\cap X'_l$ are\nlocally closed (an intersection of two locally closed sets is locally\nclosed), pairwise disjoint, and cover $X$. Take as scheme on the stratum\n$X_k\\cap X'_l$ the fibre product $Z_k\\times_XW_l$ with the immersion\n$Z_k\\times_XW_l\\to X$; it is an immersion, as a composite of the base\nchange of $\\kappa_l$ with $\\iota_k$, and its image is\n$\\iota_k(\\iota_k^{-1}(X'_l))=X_k\\cap X'_l$. This stratification refines\nboth given ones.",
   "uses": [],
   "elementary": null
  }
 ],
